{
  "title": "RFC-0007 WP2 - the graph contract's schema vocabulary: what the gate accepts and refuses, what the validator reports",
  "description": "One file, byte-identical in the Java and Rust repositories. 'compile' cases run the schema compiler on one part (body, header) or on a node's whole 'schema' property (contract): 'ok' or the exact refusal. 'validate' cases run a compiled contract against an input.body and input.header and pin every violation in order. 'report' cases pin the one-line message with its cap.",
